<section class="relative py-20 px-6 overflow-hidden">
  <div class="absolute top-[-80px] left-[8%] w-[240px] h-[240px] bg-[#636863]/30 rounded-full blur-[90px]"></div>

  <div class="absolute bottom-[-100px] right-[6%] w-[260px] h-[260px] bg-[#D3DCD3]/60 rounded-full blur-[100px]">
  </div>

  <div class="relative z-10 max-w-6xl mx-auto">

    <div class="rounded-[2.5rem] overflow-hidden border border-white/20
        bg-[#D3DCD3]/25 shadow-[0_18px_55px_rgba(0,0,0,0.16)]">

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-5">

        <div class="lg:col-span-3 p-8 lg:p-12 flex flex-col justify-center">
          <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 w-fit px-4 py-2 rounded-full bg-white/10 border border-white/15
                    text-[#113E14] text-[13px] tracking-[2px] font-semibold mb-6">

            <div class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-[#48AE4D]"></div>
            HORTICULTURAL CARE
          </div>


          <h2 class="text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-abril text-[#113E14] leading-tight mb-6">
            Proper Lighting
          </h2>


          <div class="text-[#f4f4f4] font-poppins text-[15px] leading-[1.9rem] max-w-xl">
            Horticultural plants grow best in areas that receive abundant sunlight and good air circulation.
            Proper lighting helps plants develop strong growth, healthy leaves, and better production of
            vegetables and fruits. The University of Minnesota explains that healthy growing conditions,
            including adequate light, are essential for successful plant development.
            <br><br>
            Plants grown in shaded areas may develop weak growth and reduced productivity. For this reason,
            the university recommends placing gardens in open spaces where plants can receive consistent light
            throughout the day.
            <br><br>
            When natural sunlight is limited, healthy plant growth can also be supported by maintaining proper watering,
            healthy soil, and good growing conditions that allow plants to use available light more efficiently.
          </div>


          <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mt-8">


            <div
              class="flex items-center gap-4 bg-white/10 border border-white/10 rounded-2xl px-4 py-3 hover:bg-white/15 transition-all duration-300">
              <div class="w-11 h-11 rounded-xl bg-[#48AE4D]/20 flex items-center justify-center">
                <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/resources/images/care/11.png" alt="sun icon" class="w-6 h-6 object-contain">
              </div>

              <div>
                <div class="text-white text-sm font-semibold">
                  Natural Light
                </div>

                <div class="text-white/70 text-[12px]">
                  Healthy daily growth
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>


            <div
              class="flex items-center gap-4 bg-white/10 border border-white/10 rounded-2xl px-4 py-3 hover:bg-white/15 transition-all duration-300">

              <div class="w-11 h-11 rounded-xl bg-[#48AE4D]/20 flex items-center justify-center">

                <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/resources/images/care/ll.png" alt="light icon" class="w-6 h-6 object-contain">
              </div>

              <div>
                <div class="text-white text-sm font-semibold">
                  Artificial Light
                </div>

                <div class="text-white/70 text-[12px]">
                  Perfect indoors
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>


        <div class="lg:col-span-2 relative min-h-[380px]">

          <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/resources/images/care/Curly _parsley.jpg" alt="Plant lighting"
            class="absolute inset-0 w-full h-full object-cover">


          <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-black/40 via-black/5 to-transparent"></div>
          <div
            class="absolute bottom-6 left-6 bg-white/15 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/20 rounded-2xl px-5 py-4 shadow-xl">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
              <div class="w-11 h-11 rounded-xl bg-[#D3DCD3]/20 flex items-center justify-center">
                <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/resources/images/care/leaff.png" alt="leaf icon" class="w-6 h-6">
              </div>

              <div>
                <p class="text-white text-sm font-semibold">
                  8-6 Hours
                </p>

                <p class="text-white/70 text-xs">
                  Recommended light exposure
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>




<div class="w-full py-28 px-6 relative overflow-hidden">
  <div class="absolute top-0 left-[-120px] w-[320px] h-[320px] bg-white/10 blur-[120px] rounded-full"></div>
  <div class="absolute bottom-0 right-[-120px] w-[320px] h-[320px] bg-[#D9B95B]/20 blur-[120px] rounded-full"></div>

  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto relative z-10">
    <div class="text-center mb-20">
      <div
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-[#D3DCD3]/10 backdrop-blur-xl border border-white/20 text-white text-sm tracking-[0.25em] uppercase shadow-lg">
        Horticultural Care Guide
      </div>

      <h2 class="mt-8 text-5xl md:text-6xl subpixel-antialiased font-abril text-white leading-tight">
        Essential Care Tips
        <span class="text-[#113E14]">
          for Horticultural
        </span>
      </h2>

      <p class="mt-6 text-white/80 max-w-3xl mx-auto text-lg leading-relaxed">
        Learn how to maintain healthy, productive, and thriving horticultural plants with proper growing and care
        practices.
      </p>
    </div>


    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-3 gap-10">


      <div class="group relative">
        <div
          class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-white/20 to-transparent rounded-[2.5rem] blur-2xl opacity-40 group-hover:opacity-70 transition duration-500">
        </div>

        <div class="relative h-full bg-[#D3DCD3]/30 backdrop-blur-2xl border border-white/20 rounded-[2.5rem] overflow-hidden
                shadow-[0_20px_70px_rgba(0,0,0,0.18)] hover:-translate-y-2 transition-all duration-500">


          <div class="relative p-8 pb-6">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-8">

              <div
                class="w-14 h-14 rounded-2xl bg-[#113E14] text-[#D3DCD3] flex items-center justify-center text-xl font-poppins font-bold shadow-lg">
                01
              </div>
            </div>

            <h3 class="text-3xl font-poppins font-bold text-shadow-2xs text-white leading-tight">
              Proper Watering
            </h3>
          </div>


          <div class="mx-8 h-[1px] bg-white/20"></div>
          <div class="p-8">

            <p class="text-white font-semibold leading-relaxed text-shadow-sm mb-6">
              Watering is essential because plants need water
              to transport nutrients and maintain their growth.
            </p>

            <p class="text-[#636863] leading-relaxed text-sm">
              Sandy soils may need watering twice a week, while clay soils or those rich in organic matter retain
              moisture better and require less watering • They also recommend checking the soil and watering when it is
              dry two inches below the surface.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>


      <div class="group relative">

        <div
          class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-[#D9B95B]/20 to-transparent rounded-[2.5rem] blur-2xl opacity-40 group-hover:opacity-70 transition duration-500">
        </div>

        <div
          class="relative h-full bg-white/15 backdrop-blur-2xl border border-white/20 rounded-[2.5rem] overflow-hidden shadow-[0_20px_70px_rgba(0,0,0,0.18)] hover:-translate-y-2 transition-all duration-500">

          <div class="relative p-8 pb-6">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-8">
              <div
                class="w-14 h-14 rounded-2xl bg-[#113E14] text-[#D3DCD3] flex items-center justify-center text-xl font-poppins font-bold shadow-lg">
                02
              </div>
            </div>

            <h3 class="text-3xl font-poppins font-bold text-shadow-2xs text-white leading-tight">
              Soil and Nutrition
            </h3>
          </div>

          <div class="mx-8 h-[1px] bg-white/20"></div>
          <div class="p-8">
            <p class="text-white font-semibold leading-relaxed text-shadow-sm mb-6">
              It is important to properly prepare the soil and garden area before planting. It's recommend:
            </p>

            <p class="text-[#636863] leading-relaxed text-sm">
              • Using compost
              • Conducting soil tests
              • Using raised beds if drainage is poor,
              compost improves organic matter and helps the soil retain moisture.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>


      <div class="group relative">

        <div
          class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-white/20 to-transparent rounded-[2.5rem] blur-2xl opacity-40 group-hover:opacity-70 transition duration-500">
        </div>

        <div
          class="relative h-full bg-white/12 backdrop-blur-2xl border border-white/20 rounded-[2.5rem] overflow-hidden shadow-[0_20px_70px_rgba(0,0,0,0.18)] hover:-translate-y-2 transition-all duration-500">

          <div class="relative p-8 pb-6">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-8">
              <div
                class="w-14 h-14 rounded-2xl bg-[#113E14] text-[#D3DCD3] flex items-center justify-center text-xl font-poppins font-bold shadow-lg">
                03
              </div>
            </div>

            <h3 class="text-3xl font-poppins font-bold text-white  text-shadow-2xs leading-tight">
              Fertilization
            </h3>
          </div>

          <div class="mx-8 h-[1px] bg-white/20"></div>
          <div class="p-8">
            <p class="text-white font-semibold leading-relaxed text-shadow-sm mb-6">
              The usage of mulch helps retain moisture and reduces water loss. It also protects the roots and helps
              regulate soil temperature.

            </p>

            <p class="text-[#636863] leading-relaxed text-sm">

              And when vegetable plants suffer from drought, they may:
              • Produce small fruits
              • Stop producing
              • Become tough or bitterg
              • Will wither

            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>


      <div class="group relative">
        <div
          class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-white/20 to-transparent rounded-[2.5rem] blur-2xl opacity-40 group-hover:opacity-70 transition duration-500">
        </div>

        <div
          class="relative h-full bg-[#D3DCD3]/22 backdrop-blur-2xl border border-white/20 rounded-[2.5rem] overflow-hidden shadow-[0_20px_70px_rgba(0,0,0,0.18)] hover:-translate-y-2 transition-all duration-500">

          <div class="relative p-8 pb-6">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-8">

              <div
                class="w-14 h-14 rounded-2xl bg-[#113E14] text-[#D3DCD3] flex items-center justify-center text-xl font-poppins font-bold shadow-lg">
                04
              </div>

            </div>

            <h3 class="text-3xl font-black text-white leading-tight">
              Harvesting and storage
            </h3>
          </div>

          <div class="mx-8 h-[1px] bg-white/20"></div>
          <div class="p-8">
            <p class="text-white font-semibold leading-relaxed text-shadow-sm mb-6">
              Harvesting is one of the most important process, so storagin well is an important part to enjoy of the
              escence of this plants
            </p>

            <p class="text-[#636863]/100 leading-relaxed text-sm">
              We recommend to:
              • Harvesting
              • Storage
              • Preservation
              • Seed saving
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>


      <div class="group relative md:col-span-2 xl:col-span-2">
        <div
          class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-white/20 to-transparent rounded-[2.5rem] blur-2xl opacity-40 group-hover:opacity-70 transition duration-500">
        </div>

        <div
          class="relative h-full bg-[#D3DCD3]/20 backdrop-blur-2xl border border-white/20 rounded-[2.5rem] overflow-hidden shadow-[0_20px_70px_rgba(0,0,0,0.18)] hover:-translate-y-2 transition-all duration-500">
          <div class="relative p-8 pb-6">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-8">
              <div
                class="w-14 h-14 rounded-2xl bg-[#113E14] text-[#D3DCD3] flex items-center justify-center text-xl font-poppins font-bold shadow-lg">
                05
              </div>
            </div>

            <h3 class="text-3xl font-black text-white leading-tight">
              Pests and Diseases
            </h3>
          </div>

          <div class="mx-8 h-[1px] bg-white/20"></div>

          <div class="p-8">
            <p class="text-white font-semibold leading-relaxed text-shadow-sm mb-6">

              When caring for succulents, it’s important
              to keep in mind that pests aren’t very common,
              but they can still appear:

              • mealybugs
              • scale insects
              • mites

            </p>

            <p class="text-[#636863] leading-relaxed text-sm">

              To control them, they recommend:
              • wiping away pests with cotton and alcohol
              • maintaining good lighting
              • avoiding overwatering
              • constantly monitoring the plants

              <br><br>

              It is also important to know that excessive
              humidity can cause mold and rot.

            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>






